  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 10, 'Product packaging hierarchy', shows four stepped shelves of packaged goods labelled, top to bottom, PRIMARY (vials, syringes, blister packs), SECONDARY, SECONDARY OR TERTIARY, and TERTIARY (cases and pallets). Source: GS1.org. Fig. 11, 'Example of packaging variations across manufacturers', shows one PRODUCT, a paracetamol 500 mg tablet, procured from two manufacturers with different pack configurations: MFR A ships 1 case of 12 packs of 50 tablets each, and MFR B ships 1 case of 10 packs of 100 tablets each.",
